ximately 155.6 bpm) compared with patients who experienced exercise-induced angina (approximately 137.2 bpm). This indicates that maximum heart rate achieved was lower, on average, among patients with exercise-induced angina in this dataset.*"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"3222b350","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.016144,"end_time":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.019215+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.003071+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**4.\tIs there a significant difference in resting blood pressure between male and female patients?**"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":23,"id":"802ce294","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.053775Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.053338Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.069587Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.068416Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.03595,"end_time":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.071562+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.035612+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Average resting blood pressure by gender:\n"]},{"data":{"text/plain":["sex\n","0    133.083333\n","1    130.912621\n","Name: trestbps, dtype: float64"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\n","Male average: 130.91 mm Hg\n","Female average: 133.08 mm Hg\n","t-statistic: -0.949\n","p-value: 0.3443\n","There is no statistically significant difference in resting blood pressure between males and females.\n"]}],"source":["# Average resting blood pressure for each gender\n","bp_gender = data_clean.groupby(\"sex\")[\"trestbps\"].mean()\n","\n","print(\"Average resting blood pressure by gender:\")\n","display(bp_gender)\n","\n","# Separate the two groups\n","male_pressure = data_clean.loc[data_clean[\"sex\"] == 1, \"trestbps\"]\n","female_pressure = data_clean.loc[data_clean[\"sex\"] == 0, \"trestbps\"]\n","\n","# Welch's t-test\n","test_stat, p_val = ttest_ind(\n","    male_pressure,\n","    female_pressure,\n","    equal_var=False\n",")\n","\n","print(f\"\\nMale average: {male_pressure.mean():.2f} mm Hg\")\n","print(f\"Female average: {female_pressure.mean():.2f} mm Hg\")\n","print(f\"t-statistic: {test_stat:.3f}\")\n","print(f\"p-value: {p_val:.4f}\")\n","\n","if p_val < 0.05:\n","    print(\"There is a statistically significant difference in resting blood pressure between males and females.\")\n","else:\n","    print(\"There is no statistically significant difference in resting blood pressure between males and females.\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"8fdd033a","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.016453,"end_time":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.1043+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.087847+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["*The average resting blood pressure was approximately 130.91 mm Hg for male patients and 133.08 mm Hg for female patients. Although the female average was slightly higher, the Welch t-test produced a p-value of approximately 0.34. Therefore, there is no statistically significant difference in mean resting blood pressure between male and female patients in this dataset at the 5% significance level.*"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"0c5f42aa","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.016428,"end_time":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.137027+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.120599+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**5.\tWhat is the relationship between fasting blood sugar levels and the presence of heart disease?**"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":24,"id":"51c8cfb6","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.172044Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.17121Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.385693Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.384702Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.234377,"end_time":"2026-09-15T09:18:30.387844+00:00","exception":false,"start_t